      "description": "Watch Norwich City vs Burnley highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The stage was set for a fierce Championship battle, with both sides looking to make their mark on a high-stakes fixture. On August 29, 2026 , the atmosphere at the stadium crackled with anticipation as the two teams prepared for a clash that would test their resolve and tactical discipline. An Explosive Opening Exchange The match ignited almost immediately, with Mohamed Toure opening the scoring just 2 minutes in, courtesy of an assist from Jose Cordoba . The lead was short-lived, however, as Andre Brooks fired back for his side in the 5th minute, assisted by Anthony Musaba . The frantic pace continued, with Mohamed Toure netting his second of the day in the 21st minute, followed closely by a Josh Laurent strike in the 27th minute, set up by Jacob Bruun Larsen . Tension and Late Drama As the second half progressed, the match evolved into a gritty physical contest. Tactical changes saw a flurry of substitutions, while refereeing decisions came to the forefront as Andre Brooks , Anis Ben Slimane , and Zian Flemming were all cautioned. The defining moment of the final stages occurred in the 78th minute when Josh Laurent was shown a second yellow card, resulting in a red and forcing his side to finish the match with ten men. Despite a late surge of pressure from both sides, the scoreline remained level until the final whistle, concluding a pulsating encounter that kept fans on the edge of their seats."
