      "description": "Watch Burnley vs West Ham highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. Turf Moor played host to a classic encounter on August 16, 2026 , as Burnley and West Ham United faced off in a highly anticipated Championship fixture. Both sides looked to assert their dominance in a game that kept the crowd guessing until the very last whistle. West Ham Take Charge Early The visitors started with relentless intent, and it didn't take long for them to break the deadlock. In the 10th minute, Jarrod Bowen turned provider, delivering a precise ball for Max Kilman to fire home. Burnley struggled to find their rhythm in the opening stages, often thwarted by a disciplined West Ham midfield. The physical nature of the contest was evident when Mohamadou Kante received a yellow card in the 33rd minute, as the Hammers maintained their slender lead heading into the break. The Visitors Double Their Advantage The second half saw both managers turn to their benches in an attempt to swing the momentum. While James Ward-Prowse brought stability to the West Ham engine room, Burnley introduced Zeki Amdouni to spark life into their attack. However, it was the Hammers who struck again. In the 72nd minute, Manor Solomon found the back of the net to make it 0-2, leaving the home faithful stunned and the visitors seemingly in cruise control. Flemming Ignites a Dramatic Comeback With time running out, the narrative took a sudden and dramatic turn. In the 83rd minute, Burnley were awarded a penalty, which Zian Flemming coolly dispatched to give the Clarets a lifeline. The atmosphere turned electric and feisty, leading to yellow cards for both Flemming and Mads Hermansen just a minute later. As the clock ticked into stoppage time, the improbable happened. In the 90+2nd minute, Max Alleyne set up Zian Flemming , who clinical finished to complete his brace and level the scoring at 2-2. Despite a late booking for Malick Diouf , Burnley held on to secure a remarkable point from the jaws of defeat, leaving West Ham wondering how they let the win slip away."
